---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const phone = '+19255550199';
const phoneDisplay = '(925) 555-0199';
---
<Layout title="Strange Water Heater Noises Concord CA | Popping, Rumbling, Banging" description="Water heater making popping, rumbling, or banging noises in Concord, CA? Usually sediment. Professional flush and diagnosis restores quiet operation.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> → Problems → Strange Noises</div>
      <h1>Strange Water Heater Noises</h1>
      <p>Popping, rumbling, crackling, or banging from your water heater is almost always a sign of sediment or a failing component. Address it before efficiency drops further.</p>
      <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary">Schedule Diagnosis — {phoneDisplay}</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container content-block">
      <h2>What the Sounds Usually Mean</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Popping / crackling</strong> — Water trapped under sediment boils and bursts through. Classic hard-water symptom.</li>
        <li><strong>Rumbling</strong> — Heavy sediment layer at the bottom of the tank.</li>
        <li><strong>Banging / hammering</strong> — Can be water hammer in the pipes or sediment-related; also check for loose pipes.</li>
        <li><strong>High-pitched whine</strong> — Sometimes a failing element or restriction in tankless units.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>A professional flush removes the sediment. We also inspect the anode and overall tank condition while we are there.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:2rem;text-align:center"><a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary">Book a Flush &amp; Inspection</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
